  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>In the first step bromine attacks the carbon-carbon double bond by electrophilic addition reaction mechanism and forms the bromonium&nbsp;cyclic intermediate. In the presence of sodium bicarbonate carboxylic acid group present in the reactant&nbsp;converts to carboxylate ion. This carboxylate ion opens the cyclic bromonium ion ring and forms the desired product.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0016_5f1af8aeebda.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 228px;\" /></p></blockquote>"
